                <h5 scrollto-destination="164934617" data-legacyid="sec2.1.3.1" id="164934617" data-section-title="2.1.3.1. Odd–Even Index
(OEI)" class="section-title ">2.1.3.1. Odd–Even Index
(OEI)</h5>
                <div  class="">
                <div id="164934618-content" class="article-section-wrapper js-article-section js-content-section  " data-section-parent-id="164934617">
                    
                    <div class="block-child-p">According
to the report of Yuan et al., (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref14" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">14</a>) the OEI
value of a molecular graph is calculated by <a href="javascript:;" reveal-id="eq7" data-open="eq7" class="link link-ref link-reveal xref-fn js-xref-fn split-view-modal">eq 7</a>.<div class="formula-wrap" content-id="eq7"><div class="disp-formula" id="jumplink-eq7"><span class="mathFormula"></span><div class="math"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi xmlns="">OEI</mi><mo xmlns="">=</mo><mrow xmlns=""><munderover><mo form="prefix">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mrow><mrow xmlns=""><mrow><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo form="prefix">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="italic">ij</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></math></div></div><span class="label title-label">(7)</span></div>In <a href="javascript:;" reveal-id="eq7" data-open="eq7" class="link link-ref link-reveal xref-fn js-xref-fn split-view-modal">eq 7</a>, <em>m</em> is the number of vertices (a total of
carbon and nitrogen atoms) in the molecular graph and <em>S</em> indicates the derivative matrix from the distance matrix <em>D</em>. For the elements of <em>S</em>, they are the
squares of the reciprocal distances (<em>D</em><sub><em>ij</em></sub>)<sup>−2</sup>, that is, <em>S</em><sub><em>ij</em></sub> = 1/<em>D</em><sub><em>ij</em></sub><sup>2</sup> (when <em>i</em> = <em>j</em>, let 1/<em>D</em><sub><em>ij</em></sub><sup>2</sup> = 0).</div>
                </div>
                <div id="164934619-content" class="article-section-wrapper js-article-section js-content-section  " data-section-parent-id="164934617">
                    
                    <div class="block-child-p">Following are the distance matrices <em>D</em>(<em>d</em>), <em>D</em>(<em>e</em>), and <em>D</em>(<em>f</em>) of (<em>d</em>), (<em>e</em>), and (<em>f</em>) in <a href="javascript:;" reveal-id="fig3" data-open="fig3" class="link link-reveal link-table xref-fig">Figure 3</a>, and their derivative matrices <em>S</em>(<em>d</em>), <em>S</em>(<em>e</em>), and <em>S</em>(<em>f</em>), respectively.<div class="formula-wrap" content-id="ueq1"><div class="disp-formula" id="jumplink-ueq1"><span class="mathFormula"></span><div class="math"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mstyle lineleading=".25ex" rowspacing="2ex" xmlns=""><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="true">[</mo><mstyle lineleading=".25ex" rowspacing="2ex"><mrow><mstyle lineleading=".25ex" rowspacing="2ex"><mtable columnalign="left" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mstyle></mrow></mstyle><mo stretchy="true">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo linebreak="goodbreak" lspace="0em" rspace="1em">⁣</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="true">[</mo><mstyle lineleading=".25ex" rowspacing="2ex"><mrow><mstyle lineleading=".25ex" rowspacing="2ex"><mtable columnalign="left" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mt