points <em>T</em><sub>b, pred</sub> of primary amines
(RNH<sub>2</sub>) versus experimental boiling
points <em>T</em><sub>b,exp</sub> of aliphatic alcohols (ROH)
(carbon atom number range C<sub>4</sub>–C<sub>20</sub>).</p></div></div></div><div id="fig7" content-id="fig7" class="fig fig-modal reveal-modal" data-reveal="data-reveal"><div class="fig-label fig-label">Figure 7</div><div class="graphic-wrap"><a class="fig-link" href="/view-large/figure/164934667/ao3c06992_0007.svg" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-describedby="sr-fig-viewer-action"><img class="content-image js-graphic-position-float" src="https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/8/51/10.1021_acsomega.3c06992/3/m_ao3c06992_0007.svg?Expires=1791347250&amp;Signature=FMxSOipdQiPbVWOatj4uZrtrjOvWByhtAnZ0oNu0lj7XkRiRFZBRT5pobLKTxWc6De-AZhrfBeWvHoEG6~i15EmPEt4WeYhP6t4PIvuvpL7VsDWfjLe73yT61iinmTvRtrYnZ~T-lwiOhVoXNBz1wsa4u6ckWZ1-0z9pjo1iVvfB4F7Mx7Zwm2t09Q~8O~2l1Nz49axkAUcLrPe1IhQYf2jHe9QC82Ybyxl~5PzU287RtrgZa48yrcphoCzRP4PmUp1DwOi-cCG3B3-V0SKJcDxVAQgKiY1hOBQNF32kjhaj4gUyCpIV7K4K7jr6G8yfzzhSQCClmoZbZRMzZ0XKIA__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA" data-src="https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/8/51/10.1021_acsomega.3c06992/3/m_ao3c06992_0007.svg?Expires=1791347250&amp;Signature=FMxSOipdQiPbVWOatj4uZrtrjOvWByhtAnZ0oNu0lj7XkRiRFZBRT5pobLKTxWc6De-AZhrfBeWvHoEG6~i15EmPEt4WeYhP6t4PIvuvpL7VsDWfjLe73yT61iinmTvRtrYnZ~T-lwiOhVoXNBz1wsa4u6ckWZ1-0z9pjo1iVvfB4F7Mx7Zwm2t09Q~8O~2l1Nz49axkAUcLrPe1IhQYf2jHe9QC82Ybyxl~5PzU287RtrgZa48yrcphoCzRP4PmUp1DwOi-cCG3B3-V0SKJcDxVAQgKiY1hOBQNF32kjhaj4gUyCpIV7K4K7jr6G8yfzzhSQCClmoZbZRMzZ0XKIA__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA" alt="Figure 7. Refer to the image caption for details." path-from-xml="ao3c06992_0007.svg" /></a><div class="fig-orig original-slide"><a section="164934667" class="fig-view-orig at-figureViewLarge" role="button" href="/view-large/figure/164934667/ao3c06992_0007.svg" path-from-xml="ao3c06992_0007.svg" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-label="View large Figure 7.">View Large</a><a section="164934667" href="//acs.silverchair-cdn.com/DownloadFile/DownloadImage.aspx?image=https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/8/51/10.1021_acsomega.3c06992/3/ao3c06992_0007.svg?Expires=1791347250&Signature=wTx0sx5H7A1Z6-pBMkmEZesuA0T~rDMoUPKOydJ81EQ7LlgZ8HsL1tgyas3Va0w6zx1AoCLd9ZxbBYaUFCoOkKxOq8X92o6RCsaGqVO-Qcz-IxiuX37mf0OhSLXp93The2O9I~nqkIemt9LOT6eal0XK-uxzZuwm6vNll8ZZt-uHk4x6rTdFKSn7MdBKmoQUc7KPXBNkfXYVV3lXdGVewz0BnPB1OVqMM~39EOZ6a9wKo7wLVYjpwo6DlEYZ9XSG79KfH037sQGRcPJJYYBK~EckKVR2VOmrEXNIus7CjQsSDPJT2fEwd8ffDp5XA1X1zMMTh3DvhZgy-WWZPL6Rog__&Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA&sec=164934667&ar=341563&xsltPath=~/UI/app/XSLT&imagename=&siteId=1000073" class="download-slide stats-download-slide js-download-file-gtm-datalayer-event" role="button" data-filetype="ppt" path-from-xml="ao3c06992_0007.svg" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-label="Download slide for Figure 7.">Download to Slide</a></div></div><div class="graphic-bottom"><div class="label fig-label">Figure 7.</div><div class="caption fig-caption"><p>Plot of predicted boiling
points <em>T</em><sub>b, pred</sub> of primary amines
(RNH<sub>2</sub>) versus experimental boiling
points <em>T</em><sub>b,exp</sub> of aliphatic alcohols (ROH)
(carbon atom number range C<sub>4</sub>–C<sub>20</sub>).</p></div></div><a class="close-reveal-modal" href="javascript:;"><i class="icon-general-close" aria-hidden="true"> </i><span class="screenreader-text">Close Figure 7.</span></a></div>
                </div>
                <div id="164934668-content" class="article-section-wrapper js-article-section js-content-section  " data-section-parent-id="164934658">
                    
                    <p>We noticed that the experimental boiling points
of dioctadecanamine
(C<sub>36</sub>H<sub>75</sub>N) and tridodecylamine (C<sub>36</sub>H<sub>75</sub>N) are 541.15 K (2 mmHg) and 493.15 K (0.03 mmHg) in
the literature, (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref12" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">12</a>) respectively, which are
the boiling point values under reduced pressure. Their normal boiling
points, calculated by this work, are 788.42 and 757.44 K, respectively.</p>
                </div>
                <div id="164934669-content" class="article-section-wrapper js-article-section js-content-section  " data-section-parent-id="164934658">
                    
                    <p>Additionally, we also noticed that the liquid densities (g cm<sup>–3</sup>, 293.15 K) of heptadecanamine (C<sub>17</sub>H<sub>37</sub>N) and octadecanamine (C<sub>18</sub>H<sub>39</sub>N), reported
in the literature, (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref12" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">12</a>) are 0.8510 and 0.8618,
respectively. However, the calculated values in this work are 0.8154
and 0.8171, respectively. To verify the rationality of the calculated
values, we plotted the experimental and calculated densities of <em>n</em>-alkyl primary amines against the carbon atom numbers respectively,
and obtained <a href="javascript:;" reveal-id="fig8" data-open="fig8" class="link link-reveal link-table xref-fig">Figure 8</a>. It is observed, from <a href="javascript:;" reveal-id="fig8" data-open="fig8" class="link link-reveal link-table xref-fig">Figure 8</a>, that the experimental densities of <em>n</em>-alkyl
primary amines (C<sub>1</sub>–C<sub>16</sub>) steadily increase
with the increase of carbon atom number, while the densities of heptadecanamine
(C<sub>17</sub>) and octadecanamine (C<sub>18</sub>) suddenly increase,
which is not reasonable. However, the calculated densities of <em>n</em>-alkyl primary amines steadily increase going from carbon
atom C<sub>1</sub> to C<sub>18</sub>, showing a regular change, which
is reasonable, that is, the liquid densities of heptadecanamine and
octadecanamine should be 0.8154 and 0.8171, respectively. Maybe the
values of 0.8510 and 0.8618 were entered incorrectly by the editor
of the literature. (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref12" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">12</a>)</p>
                </div>
                <div id="164934670-content" class="article-section-wrapper js-article-section js-content-section  " data-section-parent-id="164934658">
                    
